  "id": "atrial-flutter",
  "term": "atrial flutter",
  "definition": "Atrial flutter is a cardiac rhythm disorder, grouped with atrial fibrillation as one of the more common heart-rhythm problems. In the mental-health context of this source, it is discussed because stress and personality traits may be related to how it develops and how it progresses clinically.",
